      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015 Japan Pediatric Society.",
        "AbstractText": "Aortic dissection is extremely rare in children. Although it usually presents with severe chest pain, atypical clinical presentations mimicking various illnesses may cause misdiagnosis. In this report, the case of a 14-year-old boy with symptoms suggestive of acute abdomen, which was finally diagnosed as aortic dissection, is discussed."
      },
